    {
      "id": "tutorial-interface-panels-and-menus-s5",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Check yourself",
      "position": {
        "x": 930,
        "y": 460
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 560,
      "data": {
        "title": "Check yourself",
        "body": "**Challenge**\n\n1. Pick a simple authoring task.\n2. Say which panel or menu you would open first and why.\n3. Change your selection and explain whether the answer changes.\n4. Distinguish a graph-local edit from a global app control.\n5. Return to the graph surface if you are using a panel for the wrong question.\n\n**Checkpoint**\n\nYou are done when you can say:\n- legend and elements help me discover and create\n- properties help me inspect and edit the selected thing\n- menus, theme, and account controls act at a broader app level\n- I can usually tell which surface to open based on the kind of question I am asking",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "tutorial-interface-panels-and-menus"
        },
